Z||000002||Child Of Rod||09-16-2000||07:52 PM||||I got a 10.21 @148 in my 66 mustang...351w built, dual turbos, racing slicks.<BR>Too bad it was major cop bait. I was pulled over 5 times in a week, thats when I decided to sell it.  I am using the money wisely though....getting more fiero's!!!<BR>Now I just need to be able to fund the 3.4 swap into my new(to me) blue 87gt(gotta pick it up reeeeeeaaaal soon)<BR>Sorrel||||reg||6
Z||000003||hugh||09-17-2000||06:06 PM||||What was wrong?At 148mph you should have a much better et.Do you know your weight?148 mph in that car means some major horsepower. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Child Of Rod||09-18-2000||04:24 PM||||Well the weight of the mustang was about 1800-1900 pounds considering alot of it was removed and replaced with fiberglass.  <BR>Lets see a small list:<BR>Fiber hood<BR>Fiber fenders<BR>Plastic for glass<BR>1 seat<BR>floors were cut out and then welded bars across the bottom(added 50 lbs)<BR>all of the interior minus a seat was removed<BR>(carpet, sound insul, plastic bits and pieces, dashboard)<BR>Everyone thought the car would crumple, or twist itself. <BR>I really have no idea how much horsepower the engine made...my ex-friend and I built it, he was the engine head, it was just my car.  Heck ifI knew how to build engines I would have a better one in my fiero.<P>All this talk is starting to make me miss the Mustang.  Oh well maybe I will have a hotrod Fiero someday.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||HugGRRRFiero||09-18-2000||04:37 PM||||My best 1/4 mile time is in a Pro Stock class Firebird, 6.85 @ 204 mph.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">       <BR>       <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||6
