Z||000013||batboy||09-19-2000||03:41 PM||||Lar, is that a new NHRA record? I think the first official 300+ MPH run was at Heartland Park Dragstrip in Topeka (by John Force maybe?) My fastest time was in the low 13's with my 68 Chevelle SS 396 (with street tires) back in the early 80's, but I was always nervous at the track, never was fluid, and made mistakes. However, I beat several cars on the street that had much lower ET timeslips. I was totally gonzo at the stoplight grand prix and was ruthless. My baby had a radically built big block in front of a Muncie close ratio 4 speed with a Mr. Gasket vertical-gate racing shifter. People told me they never saw anyone who could shift so fast. Almost 20 years later, I sure wish I still had those lightning fast reflexes now (sigh).<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 09-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||hugh||09-19-2000||07:09 PM||||Kenny Bernstein was the 1st to run 300mph in the 1/4.I think in the early 90's.John Force was neither the 1st into the 4's,or over 300mph in a funny car.But he currently holds both ends of the record(324mph--4.8 seconds)It amazes me that the fuel cars are going faster in the 1/8th mile now than they did in the 1/4 15 years ago(over 250mph)Fuel driver Schumacher has consistently run over 320mph and is the only person to ever run 330mph in the 1/4. ||||reg||1
Z||000015||whamel||09-19-2000||10:41 PM||||F16 on takeoff for my final comp flight in the air force - pilot trying to make me lose my lunch for all the cr*p I gave him during his tour.  I have no idea what the 1/4 time would be on that, but I sure couldn't measure it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I sure miss that job sometimes!<BR>Later,<BR>Wade||||reg||1
Z||000016||BBBAD GT||09-19-2000||11:43 PM||||Fastest I've gone in my blown 5.0 that I built from the ground up is 11.13 @ 127 at 3400lb (here is the actual run <A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/Quartermile.asf" TARGET=_blank>http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/Quartermile.asf</A>  , timeslip at <A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/TimeSlip.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/TimeSlip.jpg</A>  ).  The ET is sorta high for the MPH, but I don't own a trailer and drove to the strip 100 miles one way.  This is the reason why when people ask me if my new V8 Fiero is fast, I say "its ok".  <P>I've been in several 9 sec Stangs, but only consider what I've built to be relivent.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">    <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
